  "definition": "Kul takes the SAME trades as the bot (same entry and exit times, same stop/target levels) but picks the side with his paw: a seeded coin flip per trade.",
  "mirror": "When the paw disagrees with the bot, the trade is mirrored: the raw price move flips sign, the cat still pays the same costs (commission + 1 tick slippage per fill), and the trade's worst open loss becomes the bot's best open profit (MFE) seen from the cat's fill.",
  "formula": "gross_cat = paw*side*(gross_bot + slipRT) - slipRT; MAE_cat = MFE_bot + slipRT (slipRT = 2 ticks: NQ $10, ES $25, GC $20 per mini)",
